title: August 2023

@august_lists
# prose-audit: Grade A — Nine routes that each cost something nameable: shelter inside somebody else's registration, dignity bought at eight percent, a request to Razem that reverses twenty years of the same conversation, or a PiS list that has to be explained to everyone who joined after the Tribunal ruling. The terms step and the committees' answer are now written rather than tabulated.
title: The October list negotiation
subtitle: Host-party control at 5%, coalition autonomy at 8%, and partners who can walk away
face-image: img/poland/events/sejm-column-hall.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 20
order: 10
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2023 and month = 8
on-arrival: {!
Q.third_way_active = 1;
Q.sejm_list_negotiation_done = 0;
Q.sejm_list_has_partners = 0;
Q.sejm_list_terms_code = 0;
Q.sejm_list_partner_score = 0;
Q.sejm_list_internal_score = 0;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left opens talks over the legal form of its October list";
!}
go-to: poland_sld_populist.list_filing if sld_populist_route_active = 1 and sld_populist_settlement_stage = 4 and sld_populist_orientation != "unsettled" and sld_populist_escalation != "unsettled"

= August 2023 — Five percent or eight?

A party committee clears **5%**, but its host controls nominations and the
public subsidy. We can instead ask separate parties to create a coalition
committee: each keeps its identity and a claim on funding, but all of us must
clear **8%**. The safer threshold therefore comes with the hardest terms.

The talks can include KO and the democratic parties, Third Way or one of its
hosts, PiS, independent Razem and compatible minor-left breakaways. A revived
SLD will not return through Razem, and PPS insists on its own committee if it
has already left.

[? if left_merger_structure = "federation": Our federal constitution already
contains a candidate rule, finance formula and local organising settlement.
Because its member parties retain separate legal identities, it **must file an
8% coalition committee**. The 5% host-list routes are not available unless the
federation first becomes one party.?]

- @list_target_left_host
- @list_target_left_coalition
- @list_target_razem_host
- @list_target_democratic
- @list_target_ko_host
- @list_target_third_way
- @list_target_third_host
- @list_target_pis_host
- @list_target_alone

@list_target_left_host
title: Host compatible partners on Lewica's party list
subtitle: 5% threshold and maximum control; autonomous parties will demand expensive guarantees.
view-if: left_merger_structure != "federation"
on-arrival: sejm_list_target = "Lewica host list"; sejm_list_candidate_outcome = "left_5"; sejm_list_candidate_structure = "Host-party list"; sejm_list_candidate_host = "left"; sejm_list_candidate_threshold = 5; sejm_list_candidate_members = "Lewica with any partners willing to accept host control"

We offer to be the host. Everyone stands on Lewica's registered list, we clear
five percent rather than eight, and the committee's nominations and subsidy run
through our office.

Razem's negotiators understand the offer perfectly: shelter from the threshold
in exchange for existing, legally, inside somebody else's party. They will
want that paid for in winnable places and written guarantees, and they are
entitled to.

- @list_terms: Open the terms

@list_target_left_coalition
title: Form an autonomous coalition of Left parties
subtitle: 8% threshold; partners retain identities, subsidy claims and bargaining power.
on-arrival: sejm_list_target = "Autonomous Left coalition"; sejm_list_candidate_outcome = "left_coalition_8"; sejm_list_candidate_structure = "Coalition committee"; sejm_list_candidate_host = "left_coalition"; sejm_list_candidate_threshold = 8; sejm_list_candidate_members = "Lewica, Razem and compatible minor-left parties"

We propose a coalition committee: every party keeps its registration, its name
on the ballot and its own claim on the subsidy. Nobody is anybody's guest.

The price is printed in the electoral code. A coalition committee needs eight
percent, not five, and the last four polls have put the combined Left between
seven and eleven. We are proposing to make dignity a threshold risk and asking
our partners to accept it with us.

- @list_terms: Open the terms

@list_target_razem_host
title: Ask to enter independent Razem's party list
subtitle: 5% threshold; Razem controls the list. SLD and PPS remain outside.
view-if: left_merger_structure != "federation"
choose-if: razem_party_formed = 1
unavailable-subtitle: Razem has not broken free as an independent electoral party.
on-arrival: sejm_list_target = "Razem host list"; sejm_list_candidate_outcome = "razem_5"; sejm_list_candidate_structure = "Host-party list"; sejm_list_candidate_host = "razem"; sejm_list_candidate_threshold = 5; sejm_list_candidate_members = "Razem, the coordinating Left and compatible breakaways"

We ask to stand on Razem's list. It is the smaller party, the younger one and
the one that spent years refusing exactly this kind of arrangement — and it now
holds a registration that clears five percent.

Zandberg's people do not gloat, which is worse. They ask what the old party
apparatus expects to receive and how many of its regional secretaries expect to
be nominated. SLD veterans discover what it feels like from the other side of
the table.

- @list_terms: Open the terms

@list_target_democratic
title: Propose one democratic coalition committee
subtitle: KO, Third Way and the Left keep their parties, but the combined list must clear 8%.
on-arrival: sejm_list_target = "Broad democratic coalition"; sejm_list_candidate_outcome = "democratic_8"; sejm_list_candidate_structure = "Coalition committee"; sejm_list_candidate_host = "democratic_list"; sejm_list_candidate_threshold = 8; sejm_list_candidate_members = "KO, Poland 2050, PSL and the coordinating Left"

We propose the whole democratic opposition on one committee: KO, Third Way and
the Left, one ballot line, one campaign against PiS.

Tusk has wanted this for a year. What he has not wanted is the eight percent
threshold that a coalition committee carries, or a negotiation in which PSL and
Poland 2050 hold vetoes over his candidate lists. Our proposal is simultaneously
the thing he has demanded and the version of it he likes least.

- @list_terms: Open the terms

@list_target_ko_host
title: Seek places on KO's party list
subtitle: 5% threshold and a strong ballot; KO controls nominations and subsidy.
view-if: left_merger_structure != "federation"
on-arrival: sejm_list_target = "KO host list"; sejm_list_candidate_outcome = "ko_5"; sejm_list_candidate_structure = "Host-party list"; sejm_list_candidate_host = "ko"; sejm_list_candidate_threshold = 5; sejm_list_candidate_members = "KO with Lewica candidates"

We ask KO for places on its list. Five percent, a strong ballot line and the
largest campaign machine in the democratic camp, in exchange for our candidates
being nominated by Donald Tusk's committee.

Our own organisers can do this arithmetic without help. It is the safest
available route into the Sejm and the one that ends with no Left party on the
ballot paper at all — only Left politicians on somebody else's.

- @list_terms: Open the terms

@list_target_third_way
title: Ask to expand Third Way into a three-party coalition
subtitle: 8% threshold; both PSL and Poland 2050 must consent.
on-arrival: sejm_list_target = "Expanded Third Way coalition"; sejm_list_candidate_outcome = "third_way_8"; sejm_list_candidate_structure = "Coalition committee"; sejm_list_candidate_host = "third_way"; sejm_list_candidate_threshold = 8; sejm_list_candidate_members = "PSL, Poland 2050 and the coordinating Left"

We ask Hołownia and Kosiniak-Kamysz to make their two-party committee a
three-party one. It would give the centre a social flank and give us a route
that is neither Tusk's list nor a threshold gamble alone.

Both principals have to agree, and PSL's county barons have spent two decades
explaining to their voters what the Left is. The eight percent threshold now
covers three electorates that share no obvious voter.

- @list_terms: Open the terms

@list_target_third_host
title: Seek a 5% host list from PSL or Poland 2050
subtitle: The friendlier host gains control, while the other Third Way partner may veto the rupture.
view-if: left_merger_structure != "federation"
on-arrival: sejm_list_target = "Third Way host-party list"; sejm_list_candidate_outcome = "third_host_5"; sejm_list_candidate_structure = "Host-party list"; sejm_list_candidate_host = "third_host"; sejm_list_candidate_threshold = 5; sejm_list_candidate_members = "Lewica and the more receptive Third Way party"

We approach whichever half of Third Way is likelier to take us — a five percent
host list under PSL's registration or Poland 2050's, with their control of
nominations and subsidy.

It is an offer to break somebody else's alliance in order to shelter inside the
wreckage. The partner not approached will hear about it within the day, and may
decide that the pact is worth less than the insult.

- @list_terms: Open the terms

@list_target_pis_host
title: Negotiate places on the PiS party list
subtitle: 5% threshold and host control; only a far-right Lewica can ratify the bargain.
view-if: left_merger_structure != "federation"
on-arrival: sejm_list_target = "PiS host list"; sejm_list_candidate_outcome = "pis_5"; sejm_list_candidate_structure = "Host-party list"; sejm_list_candidate_host = "pis"; sejm_list_candidate_threshold = 5; sejm_list_candidate_members = "PiS with Lewica candidates"

We ask Kaczyński's committee for places. Five percent, host control, and a
campaign in which Lewica candidates appear beneath the party that appointed
Przyłębska and wrote the disciplinary chamber.

Whatever this buys, it is not deniable. Every organiser who joined after the
Tribunal ruling now has to be told why the shortest route back to the Sejm runs
through the people who caused it.

- @list_terms: Open the terms

@list_target_alone
title: End the talks and run an independent Lewica party list
subtitle: 5% threshold, full control and no partner transfers.
view-if: left_merger_structure != "federation"
on-arrival: sejm_list_target = "Independent Lewica list"; sejm_list_candidate_outcome = "left_5"; sejm_list_candidate_structure = "Host-party list"; sejm_list_candidate_host = "left"; sejm_list_candidate_threshold = 5; sejm_list_candidate_members = "Lewica alone"; sejm_list_terms_code = 5

We end the talks. Lewica registers its own party list, clears five percent or
does not, and answers to nobody about its candidates, its programme or its
money.

The districts are told to prepare slates by themselves. There will be no
transfers, no shelter and no shared campaign — and for the first time since
2019, no argument about whose name goes above the ballot.

- @list_resolution: File the committee

@list_terms
title: What do you put on the table?
new-page: true

= What do we put on the table?

The approach to **[+ sejm_list_target +]** has been made. It would be filed as
a **[+ sejm_list_candidate_structure +]** and would have to clear **[+
sejm_list_candidate_threshold +]%**.

That settles the arithmetic and nothing else. Committees are not persuaded by
thresholds; they are persuaded by what they are being offered in exchange for
their registration, their candidates and their share of the state subsidy. Our
negotiators have one document to write and four things they could put in it.

- @list_terms_equal
- @list_terms_places
- @list_terms_programme
- @list_terms_command

@list_terms_equal
title: Share subsidy, nominations and a post-election council
subtitle: Partners prefer enforceable autonomy; the SLD apparatus loses control.
on-arrival: sejm_list_terms_code = 1; sejm_list_terms = "Shared subsidy, nominations and council vetoes"; barons_dissent += 6; party_unity += 2

We put shared subsidy, shared nominations and a post-election council on the
table: enforceable autonomy, audited, with a mechanism for settling disputes
after the votes are counted rather than during the campaign.

Partners like it because it is the only offer that does not require trusting
us. The SLD apparatus dislikes it for precisely the same reason — an audited
formula is a formula that cannot be adjusted in a back office in October.

- @list_resolution: Put the terms to the committees

@list_terms_places
title: Guarantee winnable places with an audited regional formula
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Concrete seats improve acceptance without a programme veto.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The campaign cannot administer and enforce the allocation.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; sejm_list_terms_code = 2; sejm_list_terms = "Audited safe-place guarantees"; local_network += 2; turnout_readiness += 2

We offer numbers instead of principles: named winnable places, allocated by a
published regional formula, audited by somebody neither side appoints.

It is expensive to administer and it is what negotiators actually want. A
partner can take a seat guarantee to its members; nobody has ever been able to
take a commitment to mutual respect to a regional conference.

- @list_resolution: Put the terms to the committees

@list_terms_programme
title: Offer a binding minimum programme and free votes outside it
subtitle: Helps ideological partners; adds two campaign promises.
on-arrival: sejm_list_terms_code = 3; sejm_list_terms = "Binding minimum programme and free votes"; budget_promises += 2; party_unity += 1; razem_cooperation += 3

We offer a binding minimum programme — housing, labour law, public services —
and free votes on everything outside it. The ideological partners get a reason
to sign that is not arithmetic.

Two of the commitments are more than the next Sejm is likely to fund. We have
bought agreement now with promises that will be quoted back to us in the first
budget, and everyone signing knows it.

- @list_resolution: Put the terms to the committees

@list_terms_command
title: Demand central control and offer only campaign visibility
subtitle: Preserves leadership power; autonomous partners are likely to refuse.
on-arrival: sejm_list_terms_code = 4; sejm_list_terms = "Central control with campaign visibility"; barons_dissent -= 5; party_unity -= 3

We offer visibility and keep command: our nominations, our subsidy, our
campaign, and a prominent place for partners in the advertising.

It is the offer a leadership makes when it believes the others have nowhere
else to go. Sometimes that is true. When it is not, the negotiation ends and
the party finds out in September how many districts it can staff alone.

- @list_resolution: Put the terms to the committees

@list_resolution
title: The committees answer
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
const clampListScore = function(value) {
    return Math.max(0, Math.min(100, value));
};
const relation = function(quality, fallback) {
    return Number.isFinite(Number(Q[quality])) ? Number(Q[quality]) : fallback;
};
const fit = function(otherRight) {
    return 100 - Math.abs(
        (Number(Q.left_right_score) || 35) - otherRight
    );
};
const liveFederation = String(Q.left_merger_structure) == "federation";
if (liveFederation && Number(Q.sejm_list_candidate_threshold) != 8) {
    Q.sejm_list_target = "Autonomous Left coalition";
    Q.sejm_list_candidate_outcome = "left_coalition_8";
    Q.sejm_list_candidate_structure = "Coalition committee";
    Q.sejm_list_candidate_host = "left_coalition";
    Q.sejm_list_candidate_threshold = 8;
    Q.sejm_list_candidate_members = "Lewica's federated member parties";
}
const outcome = String(Q.sejm_list_candidate_outcome || "left_5");
const coalitionForm = Number(Q.sejm_list_candidate_threshold) == 8;
let federalListBonus = 0;
if (liveFederation && coalitionForm) {
    federalListBonus += Q.federation_candidate_rule == "Joint federal primary"
        ? 8
        : (Q.federation_candidate_rule == "Rotating member-party candidacy"
            ? 5
            : (Q.federation_candidate_rule == "Inter-party delegate bargain"
                ? -3
                : -7));
    federalListBonus += Q.federation_finance_model == "Audited common treasury"
        ? 6
        : (Q.federation_finance_model == "Matched member-party budgets"
            ? 3
            : (Q.federation_finance_model == "SLD-hosted federal assets"
                ? -3
                : -5));
    federalListBonus +=
        Q.federation_membership_model == "Reciprocal organising passport"
            ? 5
            : (Q.federation_membership_model == "Territorial party specialisation"
                ? 3
                : (Q.federation_membership_model == "Parallel member-party branches"
                    ? -5
                    : -4));
    federalListBonus += Q.federation_successful ? 4 : 0;
    federalListBonus -= (Number(Q.federation_veto_pressure) || 0) * 0.6;
    federalListBonus -= (Number(Q.federation_brand_dilution) || 0) * 0.4;
} else if (liveFederation) {
    // A host-party committee places nominations and subsidy under one legal
    // owner, contradicting the federal compact rather than benefiting from it.
    federalListBonus = -6 -
        (Number(Q.federation_veto_pressure) || 0) * 0.8 -
        (Number(Q.federation_brand_dilution) || 0) * 0.5;
}
Q.sejm_list_federal_bonus = Math.round(federalListBonus);
const termPartner = Q.sejm_list_terms_code == 1 ? 14 :
    (Q.sejm_list_terms_code == 2 ? 10 :
        (Q.sejm_list_terms_code == 3 ? 8 :
            (Q.sejm_list_terms_code == 4 ? -12 : 0)));
const termInternal = Q.sejm_list_terms_code == 1 ? -2 :
    (Q.sejm_list_terms_code == 2 ? 3 :
        (Q.sejm_list_terms_code == 3 ? 6 :
            (Q.sejm_list_terms_code == 4 ? 5 : 0)));
const structurePartner = (coalitionForm ? 10 : -8) + federalListBonus;
let partnerScores = [];
let partnerNames = [];
let internalScore =
    76 - (Number(Q.internal_dissent) || 0) * 0.42 -
    (Number(Q.faction_vetoes) || 0) * 5 + termInternal +
    (liveFederation ? federalListBonus * 0.5 : 0);
let host = String(Q.sejm_list_candidate_host || "left");
const optionalMinorLeft = [
    {id: "spring", name: "Wiosna", list: "spring_breakaway"},
    {id: "labor", name: Q.labor_party_name || "Independent Labour Left", list: "labor_left"},
    {id: "progressives", name: Q.progressives_party_name || "Young Left", list: "young_left"}
].filter(function(party) {
    return !!Q[party.id + "_party_formed"];
});
const minorLeftScores = {};
const socialPatriotVote = Number(Q.social_patriot_vote_intent) ||
    Number(Q.social_patriot_poll) || 0;
const socialPatriotNeedsHost =
    !!Q.social_patriot_party_formed && socialPatriotVote < 5;

if (outcome == "left_5") {
    if (Q.sejm_list_terms_code == 5) {
        partnerScores = [100];
        partnerNames = ["Lewica campaign committee"];
    }
} else if (outcome == "left_coalition_8") {
    partnerScores = [
        42 + (Number(Q.razem_cooperation) || 0) * 0.35 +
            structurePartner + termPartner
    ];
    partnerNames = ["Razem"];
} else if (outcome == "razem_5") {
    partnerScores = [
        35 + (Number(Q.razem_cooperation) || 0) * 0.40 +
            fit(Number(Q.razem_right_score) || 18) * 0.18 +
            12 + termPartner
    ];
    partnerNames = ["Razem national council"];
    internalScore -= 12;
} else if (outcome == "democratic_8") {
    partnerScores = [
        relation("ko_relation", 40) * 0.55 +
            relation("ko_coalition_openness", 45) * 0.25 +
            fit(Number(Q.ko_right_score) || 50) * 0.20 +
            structurePartner + termPartner,
        relation("psl_relation", 25) * 0.55 +
            relation("psl_coalition_openness", 35) * 0.25 +
            fit(Number(Q.psl_right_score) || 59) * 0.20 +
            structurePartner + termPartner,
        relation("p2050_relation", 30) * 0.55 +
            relation("p2050_coalition_openness", 40) * 0.25 +
            fit(Number(Q.p2050_right_score) || 52) * 0.20 +
            structurePartner + termPartner
    ];
    partnerNames = ["KO", "PSL", "Poland 2050"];
    internalScore -= 5;
} else if (outcome == "ko_5") {
    partnerScores = [
        relation("ko_relation", 40) * 0.58 +
            relation("ko_coalition_openness", 45) * 0.22 +
            fit(Number(Q.ko_right_score) || 50) * 0.20 +
            12 + termPartner
    ];
    partnerNames = ["KO executive"];
    internalScore -= 14;
} else if (outcome == "third_way_8") {
    partnerScores = [
        relation("psl_relation", 25) * 0.55 +
            relation("psl_coalition_openness", 35) * 0.25 +
            fit(Number(Q.psl_right_score) || 59) * 0.20 +
            structurePartner + termPartner,
        relation("p2050_relation", 30) * 0.55 +
            relation("p2050_coalition_openness", 40) * 0.25 +
            fit(Number(Q.p2050_right_score) || 52) * 0.20 +
            structurePartner + termPartner
    ];
    partnerNames = ["PSL", "Poland 2050"];
    internalScore -= 7;
} else if (outcome == "third_host_5") {
    const pslReception = relation("psl_relation", 25) +
        relation("psl_coalition_openness", 35) * 0.35;
    const p2050Reception = relation("p2050_relation", 30) +
        relation("p2050_coalition_openness", 40) * 0.35;
    host = pslReception >= p2050Reception ? "psl" : "p2050";
    const otherReception = host == "psl" ? p2050Reception : pslReception;
    partnerScores = [
        Math.max(pslReception, p2050Reception) * 0.70 +
            18 + termPartner,
        otherReception * 0.60 -
            (Number(Q.third_way_cohesion) || 58) * 0.20 +
            termPartner
    ];
    partnerNames = [
        host == "psl" ? "PSL host" : "Poland 2050 host",
        host == "psl" ? "Poland 2050 veto" : "PSL veto"
    ];
    internalScore -= 10;
} else if (outcome == "pis_5") {
    partnerScores = [
        relation("pis_relation", 8) * 0.58 +
            relation("pis_coalition_openness", 30) * 0.20 +
            fit(Number(Q.pis_right_score) || 61) * 0.22 +
            14 + termPartner
    ];
    partnerNames = ["PiS political committee"];
    internalScore +=
        Math.max(0, (Number(Q.left_right_score) || 35) - 44) * 0.8 - 24;
    for (const caucus of ["spring", "progressives", "razem", "pps"]) {
        if (Q[caucus + "_active"] && Q[caucus + "_in_left"]) {
            internalScore -= (Number(Q[caucus + "_strength"]) || 0) * 0.18;
        }
    }
    if (Q.labor_active && Q.labor_in_left && !Q.labor_party_formed) {
        internalScore -=
            (Number(Q.labor_movement_leverage) || 0) * 0.18;
    }
}
if (
    ["left_5", "left_coalition_8", "razem_5"].includes(outcome) &&
    Q.sejm_list_terms_code != 5
) {
    for (const party of optionalMinorLeft) {
        const survivalBonus = !coalitionForm
            ? Math.max(
                0,
                5 - (Number(Q[party.list + "_vote_intent"]) || 0)
            ) * 1.2
            : 0;
        minorLeftScores[party.id] = clampListScore(
            42 + relation(party.id + "_party_relation", 20) * 0.28 +
                structurePartner + termPartner + survivalBonus
        );
        partnerScores.push(minorLeftScores[party.id]);
        partnerNames.push(party.name);
    }
}
partnerScores = partnerScores.map(clampListScore);
internalScore = clampListScore(internalScore);
// A minor breakaway can refuse without vetoing the core committee. It joins
// only if its own arithmetic clears the acceptance line.
const requiredPartnerScores = outcome == "left_5"
    ? []
    : (["left_coalition_8", "razem_5"].includes(outcome)
        ? partnerScores.slice(0, 1)
        : partnerScores);
const partnerScore = requiredPartnerScores.length
    ? Math.min.apply(null, requiredPartnerScores)
    : 100;
const accepted = outcome == "left_5" ||
    (partnerScore >= 50 && internalScore >= 45);
const pisFriendlyFollowup =
    !liveFederation && outcome == "pis_5" && !accepted &&
    relation("pis_relation", 8) >= 45;

Q.spring_joined_razem = 0;
Q.labor_joined_razem = 0;
Q.progressives_joined_razem = 0;
Q.social_patriot_joined_razem = 0;
Q.pps_joined_razem = 0;
Q.spring_list_committee = "spring_breakaway";
Q.labor_list_committee = "labor_left";
Q.progressives_list_committee = "young_left";
Q.social_patriot_list_committee = socialPatriotNeedsHost
    ? "pis"
    : "social_patriot";
Q.social_patriot_electoral_strategy = socialPatriotNeedsHost
    ? "Protected places on the PiS party list"
    : "Independent party list above 5%";
Q.razem_list_committee = "razem";
Q.pps_list_committee = "pps";
Q.sejm_list_followup_pending = 0;
Q.sejm_list_partner_score = partnerScore;
Q.sejm_list_internal_score = internalScore;
Q.sejm_list_acceptances = partnerNames.map(function(name, index) {
    return name + " " + Math.round(partnerScores[index]) +
        (partnerScores[index] >= 50 ? " accepts" : " refuses");
}).join("; ") + "; internal ratification " + Math.round(internalScore) +
    (internalScore >= 45 ? " passes" : " fails") +
    (Q.social_patriot_party_formed
        ? "; Lewica Patriotyczna chooses " +
            Q.social_patriot_electoral_strategy
        : "") +
    (liveFederation
        ? "; federal structural modifier " +
            (Q.sejm_list_federal_bonus >= 0 ? "+" : "") +
            Q.sejm_list_federal_bonus
        : "");

if (accepted) {
    Q.sejm_list_outcome = outcome;
    Q.sejm_list_structure = String(Q.sejm_list_candidate_structure);
    Q.sejm_list_host = host;
    Q.sejm_list_threshold = Number(Q.sejm_list_candidate_threshold);
    Q.sejm_list_members = String(Q.sejm_list_candidate_members);
    Q.sejm_list_control = coalitionForm
        ? "Partners retain party identity and subsidy claims"
        : (host == "left"
            ? "Lewica controls nominations and subsidy"
            : host + " controls nominations and subsidy");
    Q.sejm_list_result = Q.sejm_list_target + " accepted";
    Q.sejm_list_has_partners = outcome == "left_5" ? 0 : 1;
    if (outcome == "left_5" && Q.sejm_list_terms_code != 5) {
        const joinedNames = [];
        for (const party of optionalMinorLeft) {
            if (minorLeftScores[party.id] >= 50) {
                Q[party.id + "_list_committee"] = "left";
                joinedNames.push(party.name);
            }
        }
        Q.sejm_list_members = ["Lewica"].concat(joinedNames).join(", ");
        Q.sejm_list_has_partners = joinedNames.length ? 1 : 0;
    } else if (outcome == "left_coalition_8") {
        const joinedNames = [];
        for (const party of optionalMinorLeft) {
            if (minorLeftScores[party.id] >= 50) {
                Q[party.id + "_list_committee"] = "left_coalition";
                joinedNames.push(party.name);
            }
        }
        if (Q.razem_party_formed) Q.razem_list_committee = "left_coalition";
        Q.sejm_list_members = ["Lewica", "Razem"].concat(joinedNames).join(", ");
    } else if (outcome == "razem_5") {
        const joinedNames = [];
        for (const party of optionalMinorLeft) {
            if (minorLeftScores[party.id] >= 50) {
                Q[party.id + "_joined_razem"] = 1;
                Q[party.id + "_list_committee"] = "razem";
                joinedNames.push(party.name);
            }
        }
        Q.sejm_list_members = ["Razem", "coordinating Left"]
            .concat(joinedNames).join(", ");
        Q.razem_alliance_arithmetic =
            "Negotiated 5% Razem host list; " +
            (joinedNames.length ? joinedNames.join(", ") + " joined; " : "") +
            "SLD and PPS remain separate";
    }
    Q.party_unity += coalitionForm ? 2 : (host == "left" ? 1 : -2);
    Q.turnout_readiness += 3;
    Q.news_headline = Q.sejm_list_result;
} else if (pisFriendlyFollowup) {
    Q.sejm_list_followup_pending = 1;
    Q.sejm_list_outcome = "left_5";
    Q.sejm_list_structure = "Host-party list";
    Q.sejm_list_host = "left";
    Q.sejm_list_threshold = 5;
    Q.sejm_list_members = "Lewica pending revised terms with PiS";
    Q.sejm_list_control = "Pending revised terms after PiS objections";
    Q.sejm_list_result =
        Q.sejm_list_target +
        " enters a final objection round instead of outright rejection";
    Q.sejm_list_has_partners = 0;
    Q.news_headline =
        "PiS asks Lewica to revise host-list terms before filing";
} else {
    Q.sejm_list_outcome = liveFederation ? "left_coalition_8" : "left_5";
    Q.sejm_list_structure = liveFederation
        ? "Coalition committee"
        : "Host-party list";
    Q.sejm_list_host = liveFederation ? "left_coalition" : "left";
    Q.sejm_list_threshold = liveFederation ? 8 : 5;
    Q.sejm_list_members = liveFederation
        ? "Lewica's federated member parties after failed outside talks"
        : "Lewica alone after failed talks";
    Q.sejm_list_control = liveFederation
        ? "Member parties retain identity and subsidy claims"
        : "Lewica controls nominations and subsidy";
    Q.sejm_list_result = Q.sejm_list_target +
        (liveFederation
            ? " rejected; the federation files its own coalition committee"
            : " rejected; Lewica files its own party list");
    Q.sejm_list_has_partners = liveFederation ? 1 : 0;
    Q.party_unity -= 3;
    Q.left_poll_momentum -= 0.2;
    Q.news_headline = Q.sejm_list_result;
}
Q.sejm_list_negotiation_done = 1;
!}

= A committee is filed

The answers come back over three days, by telephone and then in writing.
**[+ sejm_list_result +].**

[? if sejm_list_followup_pending: Nothing is registered yet. PiS has not closed
the channel; it has sent back a page of conditions on control, message
discipline and candidate guarantees, and expects an answer before it will sign
anything.?]

What is filed is a **[+ sejm_list_structure +]**, needing **[+
sejm_list_threshold +]%**, with nominations and money controlled by **[+
sejm_list_control +]**. Those three facts will shape every argument of the next
two months more than any sentence in the programme.

The electoral commission does not care how the decision was reached. From this
morning the districts stop lobbying about the shape of the ballot and start
lobbying about who is on it — the same fight, conducted by the same people, in
a room where the rules are now fixed.

SLD and PPS breakaways keep their own committees. Nothing agreed here folds
them into anyone else's.
[? if social_patriot_party_formed: **Lewica Patriotyczna:** [+
social_patriot_electoral_strategy +].?]

go-to: list_pis_objections if sejm_list_followup_pending = 1; poland_event_queue if sejm_list_followup_pending = 0

@list_pis_objections
title: PiS states objections and offers one final bargain
new-page: true

= A final host-list negotiation

PiS does not close the door outright. Its committee delivers one page of
objections: host-list discipline must be explicit, candidate places must be
ratified by the host, and campaign lines cannot contradict the bloc's core
message in key districts.

The objections are not new. They are the points we have so far refused to
fulfil. We can concede and secure entry, or refuse and file independently.

- @list_pis_objections_concede
- @list_pis_objections_refuse

