@senate_one_list_aftermath
title: The pact survives the larger argument

Donald Tusk welcomes our demand and immediately turns it against Third Way.
Hołownia and Kosiniak-Kamysz refuse to dissolve their Sejm project; Razem says
a common Senate candidate is sensible precisely because it does **not** require
one proportional list under KO's leadership.

The district map is still signed, but later and with less trust. We gain a
clear answer to the one-list question: KO agrees, while Third Way and part of
our own party do not.

- @poland_event_queue: Campaign on the answer

