KO and Third Way refuse to reopen their national formula. They do, however,
yield a handful of districts where mayors, councillors and organisers can show
that a Lewica name is the pact's strongest name.

Those candidates receive the common endorsement. The rest of the map remains
a bilateral bargain, and Czarzasty has no equal veto over it. Local roots have
won representation that the national poll could not command.

