= August 2023 — A place in Kielce

**[+ ko_leader +]**'s list committee gives **Roman Giertych** a winnable place
in Kielce. The
Senate pact, negotiated district by district between KO, Third Way and
ourselves, gives him nothing at all — and the reason is not a shortage of
districts. A Senate candidate is one name in one constituency, endorsed by
every party in the pact. Nobody wanted to endorse this one.

Our own club chair, **Anna Maria Żukowska**, says it out loud on 11 August:
*if he were as well-liked as everyone claims, somebody would have put him
forward for the senate pact* — and nobody did, because a joint candidate's
votes on partnerships and abortion become everybody's votes. She adds the line
that will be quoted back at this coalition for years: *despite his
declarations, he has not changed that much.*

What he was is not in dispute. He led the **League of Polish Families** out of
the **All-Polish Youth**, and in 2006 he was deputy prime minister and minister
of education in Jarosław Kaczyński's cabinet — reading lists purged, a national
campaign against what he called homosexual propaganda in schools, uniforms and
discipline promised for every classroom. What he is now is **[+ ko_leader +]**'s own
lawyer, a man PiS prosecutors detained in front of cameras in 2020, and the
loudest voice in the democratic camp for putting the last eight years before a
court. That is the whole of the reason he has a place: there is exactly one
person in KO who wants him there, and that person runs the list.

A Sejm list is KO's own business and a Senate pact is ours jointly. This is
only the first place where those two facts collide.

- @giertych_2023_public
- @giertych_2023_quiet
- @giertych_2023_welcome

@giertych_2023_public
title: Confirm publicly why the pact has no district for him
subtitle: Establish the reason on the record now, before anybody has to explain it after a result.
on-arrival: giertych_line = "Pact refusal stated publicly"; giertych_standing -= 6; progressive_credibility += 4; ko_relation -= 4; feminist_trust += 3; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "Lewica states why the Senate pact carries no joint candidate in Giertych's case"

Żukowska explains the mechanics rather than the man: a pact candidate is
endorsed by four parties, and our voters are entitled to know what they would
be endorsing. She lists the ministry circulars by date.

KO's press office calls it an attack on an ally under prosecution. It is also a
sentence with a timestamp, which is worth more later than any argument we could
construct after the fact.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the reason on the record

@giertych_2023_quiet
title: Keep the pact intact and say nothing about one Sejm place
subtitle: The Senate map matters more in September than a quarrel about a candidate we do not have to endorse.
on-arrival: giertych_line = "Silence during the campaign"; giertych_standing += 3; ko_relation += 3; senate_cohesion += 3; progressives_dissent += 3; progressive_credibility -= 2; news_headline = "The democratic pact avoids a public quarrel over KO's list"

Fifty-one Senate districts are worth more than one interview. We answer that
lists are each party's own responsibility, and we go back to counting seats in
Podkarpacie.

It is the correct campaign decision. It also means the first time we are asked
about him with power at stake, the archive will show us declining to answer.

- @poland_event_queue: Go back to counting districts

@giertych_2023_welcome
title: Treat him as an asset of the democratic camp
subtitle: A prosecuted opponent of PiS is useful; say so, and accept what the endorsement costs with our own people.
on-arrival: giertych_line = "Democratic-camp endorsement"; giertych_standing += 8; ko_relation += 6; ko_right_score += 2; progressives_dissent += 6; razem_dissent += 6; progressive_credibility -= 6; feminist_trust -= 3; news_headline = "Lewica calls Giertych part of the democratic camp"

We say the obvious campaign thing: the man was detained by Ziobro's people, his
files were taken in front of cameras, and the party that did it is the party we
are trying to remove. All of that is true.

Razem's press team publishes the 2006 circulars the same afternoon, without
comment, which is more effective than comment. We have spent something we will
want back in about three years.

- @poland_event_queue: Accept the endorsement
